# No consumer content in this core (hard gate)

`fynns_ui_design_core` is the design-system source of truth. Sandbox Globals /
Preview / Layout demos teach **primitive anatomy** — not any consumer product.

## Forbidden (hard)

- Importing, mirroring, or inventing demo copy from any consumer app
  (GSC Live Preview, agents-hub, thesis tools, music studio, corrector,
  **CV Generator**, LearnSpace, …)
- Consumer product UI strings (feature names, LLM providers, volume mounts,
  dataset cards, GSC script jargon, university / employer / CV résumé facts,
  app-specific settings titles, real routes, env keys, API shapes)
- Screenshots or i18n from a consumer used as “live” demo truth in sandbox /
  AGENTS / primitive defaults
- Pasting consumer settings cards / Experiences screens into Globals “as realism”
- Catalog keywords or help text that name a consumer product as the demo subject
  (e.g. `cv`, `GSC`, `Ollama` as the thing being shown — not as a forbidden-term
  note in agent docs)
- **Lettered / ranked comparison shells** as visible product UI in Globals
  (`A · flat`, `Variant B`, `Shell C`, `list-detail` as a third timeline host).
  Timeline demo = unlabeled **flat** + **with detail** only — see
  `.cursor/rules/timeline-catalog.mdc`

## Required instead

- **UI shell only:** generic placeholders that could belong to any app
  (`Sample role`, `Sample org`, `Project preferences`, `Compact`,
  `Digests`, `Region`, `sample@example.com`, …)
- Default primitive labels stay **English or German** (AGENTS.md Language)
- Consumers copy **structure** from `#form-recipe` / `#timeline` / AGENTS
  recipes and supply **their own** strings in the consumer repo

## Gate

- Cursor rule: this file (alwaysApply)
- Timeline host gate: [`.cursor/rules/timeline-catalog.mdc`](timeline-catalog.mdc) (on-demand)
- AGENTS.md Hard rules (**DON'T** paste consumer content / lettered shells)
- CI / local: `npm run check:no-consumer` (denylist scan of sandbox + demo paths)

If a demo could pass for a real consumer screen after removing chrome labels,
**rewrite it before shipping**.
